= Using the permissions class =

The [../classes/html/classpermissions.html permissions class] provides static methods for working with file permissions.

Rudiments supports unix-style file permissions, even on Windows.  The permissions class provides methods for parsing permission strings (like "rwxr-xr--") into numeric modes, converting numeric modes back to permission strings, and constructing permissions using convenience methods for common combinations.

The following example parses a permission string into a mode, converts a mode back to a string, builds permissions using convenience methods, and displays some common permission values.

